# cw103, the quiet name-keeper (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 2: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw103
revision 2
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for tn_fh_jory_rimepeak
written_by claude-codex-cw-1
title the quiet name-keeper
fits stage=adult|old
prefers talk=quiet humour=dry
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk remembers_every_name_ever_heard
likes blackberries draughts market_bustle autumn_wind
dislikes cold_tea bad_manners
fears being_forgotten empty_workbench
hopes a_room_in_ridgemere fair_wages
topics work +0.6 memories +0.5 friends +0.4 pastimes +0.3 weather +0.2 gossip -0.4
styles comfort=practical gossip=reluctant refuse=soft tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# is a quiet, dryly funny loom hand with a head full of #names#, a worn #board#, and a wish for fair work.

words
oath! = Count the threads | By the last knot
saying! = A name holds longer than a knot | The loose end always shows
shuttle = the shuttle in my paw | that little wooden runner
warp = long threads held tight | threads stretched for weaving
weft = the thread crossing back | the thread that goes across
selvedge = the edge that keeps its shape | the cloth's firm edge
bench = my place by the loom | the bench at the loom
names = names I keep in my head | names that stay with me
board = my draughts board | the board with the worn corners
pieces = the dark and pale pieces | those little playing stones
berries = berries from the hedge | black fruit off the lane
wind = wind with a cold edge | air that lifts the loose wool
quiet = a little room to think | the hush between two turns
coin = a coin earned by the hour | what a day's work brings home
city = the city down the road | Ridgemere beyond the fields

any
opinion @1 city against 1 : #city.capitalize# has work, I hear, but a crowd can make a wolf feel uncounted. | There may be wages in #city#, though I would miss knowing who sat beside me.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : A fair scale is easy to recognise. I wish more keepers used one when they reckon #coin#. | If cloth sells dear, the hands at #bench# should see more of the money.
opinion @1 times against 1 : Each week takes a little more #coin# to put supper on the table. | I count the hours, then count what #coin# they'll buy. The second number keeps shrinking.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 0 : I like hearing the music from a step away; the crush is too much for me. | A festival is fine from the edge, with a little #quiet# between the songs.
opinion @1 newcomers mixed 0 : I learn a new wolf's name before I decide what sort of neighbour that wolf will be. | A new face means another of the #names# I keep, and another pair of hands.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : A House can price a bolt of cloth without knowing who kept #selvedge# straight. | I'd trust a hand that checked the #warp# before I'd trust a crest on a door.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. I'll remember your name if you give it. | #greet#. There is room beside #board#, if you like quiet.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Let me finish this pass of #shuttle#. | #greet#. #weft.capitalize# will wander if I look away now.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. The #wind# has got here before the rest of us. | #greet#. A fresh day, and a fresh length of #warp#.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. I'd know that step even in the dark. | #greet#. #bench.capitalize# can wait until morning.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Ah, you. I kept a place by the fire. | There you are. I was beginning to count the minutes.
line @1 again.open : Twice today. I have not forgotten the first time. | Here again; your face had not gone from my mind.
line @1 greet.return : #welcome_back#. I still owe you a proper answer. | #welcome_back#. I had another thought about what you said.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Your turn at #board# is still waiting. | Come sit. I saved the good chair for you.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : Back already. This length of #warp# is nearly done. | I can speak when #shuttle# reaches the end.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Back before sleep. I thought that might be you. | Another visit after dark. I shall keep the lamp low.
line @1 farewell : #saying.capitalize#. Walk carefully. | Keep #quiet# when you can. Farewell.
line @1 farewell.return : And a safe road toward #city# to you. | I'll know your step next time. Go well.
line @2 farewell [here.time=night] : Mind the dark stones on the road to #city#. | Go gently. The lamp outside has a short reach.
line @1 react.news : #listen.capitalize#. Say that once more, while #shuttle# rests. | That is news worth putting down #shuttle# for.
line @1 react.news.new : I had not heard it. Who told you? | New to me. I'll keep that among the #names# and stories I remember.
line @1 react.news.known : I heard a little of it. Your part fills a gap among the #names# I heard. | So it has reached you too. I wondered when it would.
line @1 react.news.doubt : That account has a loose end, like a bad #selvedge#. | I would hear it from another mouth before I set it down as true.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : A hard thing to carry. I am sorry. | I can sit with you in #quiet# if you want.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good for them. I hope it lasts. | That is a bright turn of #weft#.
line @1 answer.how : Well enough, with work for my paws. | A little tired, but steady as the #warp#.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Busy. I can count #shuttle# passes better than the hours. | #weft.capitalize# has kept me here since first light.
line @1 ask.how : How has the day treated you? | And how are you holding up? I have a little #quiet# to listen.
line @1 sympathise : I will sit a while if you want company. | I heard you. We can have a little #quiet# if you need it.
line @1 reassure : One bad row of #weft# can be undone. Breathe first. | We'll see the whole cloth before we judge this bit.
line @1 decline : I cannot give that the care it needs just now; ask me after #shuttle# rests. | I would rather say no plainly than promise and leave you waiting.
line @1 accept_decline : Fair enough. No #coin# owed between us. | I asked; you answered. That will do.
line @1 thank : You spared me a difficult hour at #bench#. Thank you. | I will remember the help, and the wolf who gave it.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I had a free paw off #shuttle#. That is all. | You would have done as much for me.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : #shuttle.capitalize# is waiting for me. We can finish this later. | I must get back to #bench# before the light goes.
line @2 preclose : I should leave you a little #quiet#. | That is enough talk for one sitting, I think.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : #pieces.capitalize# move faster when I am not looking. Curious. | I could let you win at #board#, but you would spot it.
line @1 tease.return [pair.band=friends] : Keep talking; I am learning your next move. | That was almost sharp enough to cut #weft#.
line @1 ack : #bc_it_is#. | #bc_fair_enough#.
line @1 give.advice : Do the next small thing well. The rest can wait. | Leave a little slack in #weft#; a thread drawn too hard will snap.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Keep to the travelled road. Trouble has been close to #city#. | Do not take the short path alone while the roads are troubled.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : I know that walk. Come to #board#. | Your chair is free, if you want it.
scene shuttle_pause
when topic=work self.working=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #shuttle.capitalize# sticks when my mind gets ahead of my paws. | I have crossed #weft# three times and still found a fault.
b : Shall I leave you to it? | Is it worth undoing now?
a : Stay, but let me finish this row of #weft#. Then I can listen. | Better now than after a whole bolt. There, the edge lies right.

scene cloth_edge
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #selvedge.capitalize# tells you how careful a hand was. | Give me the end of a bolt and I will show you the maker's hurry.
b : I never thought to look at the edge. | Does a small flaw matter so much?
a : Most folk do not look at #selvedge#. They notice when it comes loose. | It matters when someone wears it through winter.

scene counting_names
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I keep #names# without meaning to. It began with the wolves on our street. | A stranger tells me a name once, and it sits with all the others.
b : That must fill your head. | Do you ever forget one?
a : There is room for #names#. I forget where I left my cup instead. | I forget cups and errands. Names are stubborn things.

scene draughts_corner
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #board.capitalize# has a chipped corner. It still makes a fair game. | I keep #pieces# in an old cloth bag, dark against pale.
b : Who taught you to play? | Have you lost many pieces?
a : A neighbour who never let me take a move back at #board#. A useful teacher. | Only one. I made another from a pebble, and it plays as well.

scene berries_hill
when topic=food here.season=summer|autumn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #berries# are black along the lane now. | I came home with #berries# in my pocket and a stain on my sleeve.
b : Are they sweet this year? | Did you save any for supper?
a : Some #berries# are. I eat the sour ones too, to keep the sweet ones honest. | Enough for a bowl. The rest went before I reached the door.

scene wind_in_wool
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : This #wind# gets into a bundle of wool before you can tie it. | I could hear the #wind# working at the shutters all night.
b : Did it spoil your work? | Were you able to sleep?
a : Only the bundle of wool I left loose in that #wind#. That was my doing. | Some. The shutters lost the contest before dawn.

scene held_breath
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like #quiet# after everyone has gone to supper. | There is a moment at the end of work when the whole room seems to wait.
b : Does it stay quiet long? | What are you waiting for?
a : Only until somebody remembers a last errand. Long enough for #quiet#. | Nothing. That is why I like it.

scene friend_at_board
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# can tell when I am hiding a move on #board#. | I can sit with #self.friend# for an hour and say very little.
b : Is that a good friend, then? | Is the silence comfortable?
a : A very good one. I have never had to pretend to win at #board#. | It is. Some company asks you for nothing at all.

scene spouse_evening
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.spouse# knows when I have counted too many hours at #bench#. | #self.spouse# sets a cup down beside me when I go quiet.
b : What gives you away? | That sounds like kindness.
a : I start counting steps on the walk home. It makes my #self.spouse_word# laugh. | It is. I try to notice before the cup goes cold, as #self.spouse# notices me.

scene town_names
when topic=home here.region=coldwater
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I could give you #names# for every door on this street. | Coldwater changes, but I keep #names# for the houses that stood before.
b : Would you tell me one? | Does that make leaving difficult?
a : Another day. One of those #names# deserves a whole story. | It might. I have not settled that question.

scene road_to_city
when topic=travel self.from=coldwater
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I wonder what work a hand can find in #city#. | The road to #city# is plain enough. Deciding to take it is harder.
b : Would you go alone? | What keeps you here?
a : Perhaps. A new place gives a wolf room to begin again. | Familiar faces, familiar #names#, and things I have not finished.

scene market_edge
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I watch the market from the edge. You can hear the price change from stall to stall. | I count #coin# twice before buying, and still come home with less than I hoped.
b : Do you challenge a bad price? | Does anyone get a fair bargain?
a : If I know the measure and #coin# asked. Otherwise I walk on. | Sometimes. You have to know what you are looking at.

scene thin_week
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A thin week makes every #coin# feel heavy in the paw. | I have seen a wolf put back a loaf and pretend it was a choice.
b : What can be done? | Did you say anything?
a : Start with the nearest table and see who has a spare #coin#. | No. I bought the loaf and left it where it could be found.

scene autumn_steps
when topic=season here.season=autumn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #wind# has that autumn bite again. | The first leaves gather by the door before anyone thinks to sweep.
b : Do you like this season? | Will you clear them away?
a : I do. That #wind# gives a wolf a reason to come in and sit. | After the next cup. They can wait as well as I can.

scene chapel_listen
when topic=faith
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I seek #quiet# in chapel. There is enough speaking elsewhere. | I have never asked the Bright One for a full purse.
b : What do you ask for? | What would you ask for, then?
a : Patience to hear what I missed the first time, and a little #quiet#. | A steady hand, and a kinder day for the wolves beside me.

scene name_newcomer
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A new face came through today. I shall learn the name before I learn the tale. | I heard another unfamiliar name at the well this morning.
b : You are curious, then? | Will you ask whose it is?
a : About the wolf, yes. Even the #names# I keep are only a beginning. | If we meet. I will not chase a rumour round town.

scene two_moves_ahead
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I lost at #board# by planning three moves ahead and missing the one under my nose. | A patient player can make #pieces# look foolish.
b : Will you play again? | Do you mind losing?
a : Certainly. I might notice #board# this time. | Only when I had a better move and failed to see it.

story first_game [topic=memories self.age>=25]
  : The first #board# I learned on was scratched into a tabletop.
  : We used pebbles for #pieces#, and a missing pebble meant somebody had taken a move home.
  ask : Did you ever learn a game from someone who refused to explain it?
  b : I have had a teacher like that.
  : I remember the moves better than the lesson, which may have been the lesson.

story wrong_name [topic=memories self.age>=25]
  : I once answered to the wrong name all morning rather than embarrass a tired carter.
  : By noon the whole yard used it. I finally told him, and we both laughed.
  ask : Would you have corrected him sooner?
  b : I might have. It depends on the carter.
  : Probably wise. I still remember the name he gave me.

story unruly_thread [topic=work self.working=yes]
  : One day a loose thread caught #shuttle# and stopped the loom outright.
  : I spent longer finding the knot than I would have spent doing the row again.
  ask : Would you start again, or hunt for the knot?
  b : I would have to see the cloth.
  : A fair answer. I started again, then found the knot under my sleeve.

rule @bark_board
when concept=bark here.time=dusk|night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say #board.capitalize# is out, if anyone wants a game. | One seat by #board# is free.

rule @bark_work
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Mind the #warp#; it is stretched tight. | #shuttle.capitalize# has a mind of its own today.

rule @bark_berries
when concept=bark here.season=summer|autumn
does aside
cooldown 10h
say #berries.capitalize# by the lane, if the birds have left any. | I know where the #berries# grow, and I am not telling.

rule @bark_wind
when concept=bark here.weather=storm
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Hold the door; the #wind# will have it. | There goes another bundle after the #wind#.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. I can spare a moment. What did you want to know? | #greet#. Say on; I am listening.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I remember you. What brings you back? | #topic.player#. There is a place beside me if you want to talk.
dlg @1 resident.job : I work with cloth. #selvedge.capitalize# tells me when a day has gone well. | I take #shuttle# from one edge to the other until the light fails.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Walk safely. I shall remember the visit. | #saying.capitalize#. Go well.
graft resident.hub
choice How do you remember every name? -> names
node names
say I hear a name once and it stays. I cannot do the same with where I left my cup.
mood pleased
free
choice Has that ever caused trouble? -> names_trouble
choice Thank you. -> hub
node names_trouble
say I once answered to a wrong name all morning to spare a tired carter. It took until noon to correct him.
choice Back to what we were saying. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
